<title>SPAIN: Spanish Treasury announces April bond tenders.</title>
<headline>Spanish Treasury announces April bond tenders.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain announced on Monday the amount of notes and bonds the Spanish Treasury would tender at its monthly auctions on Tuesday and Wednesday.</p>
<p>Following are the minimum and maximum amounts:</p>
<p>(in billions of pesetas)</p>
<p>ISSUE	   Expected amount   Maximum amount     Auction date</p>
<p>3 and 10-yr	275		    340		  April 1</p>
<p>5 and 15-yr	150		    190		  April 2</p>
<p>    March auctions	   amount announced   allotted</p>
<p>    1/10 (3- and 10-year)	250 - 325	353.176 *</p>
<p>    2/10 (5- and 15-year)	125 - 175	120.552 *</p>
<p>* This is the amount actually sold on the market and includes the second segment of the auction.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
